adjudication.rationale:
In `reauthenticationOfUserWithoutPasskey()` the diff adds two identical blocks:
```java
try {
  MatcherAssert.assertThat(driver.findElement(By.xpath("//form[@id='webauth']")), nullValue());
  fail("Not expected to have webauthn button");
} catch (Exception nsee) {
  // expected
}
```
This relies on `findElement` throwing to indicate absence and uses a broad `catch (Exception)` with an assertion that will never be true if an element is returned (WebElement is non-null), making the intent opaque and duplicating the pattern twice. While not a product bug, it is a concrete, diff-grounded test-quality/maintainability issue.
